1
00:04:51,818 --> 00:04:57,818
The holy terror is back!

2
00:09:43,636 --> 00:09:49,636
Sister Act 2: Back in the Habit is a music, comedy film directed by Bill Duke.

3
00:14:35,454 --> 00:14:41,454
Deloris Van Cartier is again asked to don the nun's habit to help a
run-down Catholic school, presided over by Mother Superior.

4
00:19:27,272 --> 00:19:33,272
And if trying to reach out to a class full of uninterested students wasn't bad enough, the sisters
discover that the school is due to be closed by the unscrupulous chief of a local authority.

5
00:24:19,090 --> 00:24:25,090
Deloris Van Cartier, played by Whoopi Goldberg.

6
00:29:10,909 --> 00:29:16,909
Sister Mary Patrick, played by Kathy Najimy.

7
00:34:02,727 --> 00:34:08,727
Rita Louise Watson, played by Lauryn Hill.

8
00:38:54,545 --> 00:39:00,545
Florence Watson, played by Sheryl Lee Ralph.

9
00:43:46,363 --> 00:43:52,363
Mother Superior, played by Maggie Smith.

10
00:48:38,181 --> 00:48:44,181
Father Maurice, played by Barnard Hughes.

11
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Sister Act 2: Back in the Habit is a 1993 American jukebox musical comedy
film, directed by Bill Duke, and released by Touchstone Pictures.

12
00:58:21,818 --> 00:58:27,818
A sequel to the 1992 film Sister Act, it is loosely based on the life of
Crenshaw High School choir instructor Iris Stevenson.

13
01:03:13,636 --> 01:03:19,636
The film follows Whoopi Goldberg reprising her role as Deloris Van Cartier, who
returns to assist her nun friends in saving their struggling school.

14
01:08:05,454 --> 01:08:11,454
Maggie Smith, Kathy Najimy, Wendy Makkena, and Mary Wickes
reprise their roles from the original film.

15
01:12:57,272 --> 01:13:03,272
While Sister Act 2 was a modest box office success, it was
initially panned by critics compared to its predecessor.

16
01:17:49,090 --> 01:17:55,090
However, the film gained a devoted following over time, particularly for
its energetic musical performances and uplifting themes.

17
01:22:40,909 --> 01:22:46,909
It starred Lauryn Hill in her breakout role, alongside Sheryl Lee
Ralph, Alanna Ubach, and Jennifer Love Hewitt.

18
01:27:32,727 --> 01:27:38,727
Notable members of the film's choir include R&B singer Ryan Toby of
City High and The War and Treaty singer Tanya Trotter.

19
01:32:24,545 --> 01:32:30,545
Gospel singer Erica Campbell of Mary Mary also appeared in
the film as a member of the opposing choir.

20
01:37:16,363 --> 01:37:22,363
The film explores themes of nun, education, music
competition, sequel, singing nun.

21
01:42:08,181 --> 01:42:14,181
The tone is lighthearted.
